  "strategy": "**Approach and Rationale:**  \nThe goal is to minimize the evaluation function \\( \\text{evaluate\\_sequence}(s) = 2 \\times n \\times \\text{max\\_conv}/(\\text{sum\\_a}^2) \\), where \\( \\text{max\\_conv} = \\|f * f\\|_\\infty \\) for the sequence \\( f \\). The key insight is leveraging the scale-invariance property of the objective for sequences with a fixed length (128) and a normalization factor (sum=1). A variant of the previous LP-based method combined with gradient descent is adapted for targeted optimization.\n\n**Mathematical Specification:**  \n- **Representation:** All sequences are mapped to the simplex \\( \\sum a_i = 1 \\), \\( a_i \\geq 0 \\), to ensure affine-invariance and satisfy the sum constraint.  \n- **Objective:** For normalized sequences, \\( \\|f * f\\|_\\infty \\) is scaled by \\( 2 \\times n \\), and \\( \\text{evaluate\\_sequence}(a) = 2 \\times n \\times \\text{max\\_conv} \\) (since sum(a)=1).  \n- **Constraints:** Sequences must have a sum \u2265 0.01 and be non-negative, which is handled by the projection to the simplex.  \n- **Optimization Formulation:** The problem is viewed as a smooth maximization problem where we approximate the tight bound \\( \\|f * f\\|_\\infty \\) via gradient descent on a logarithmic scale.\n\n**Implementation Procedure:**  \n1. **Initialization:**  \n   - Start with sequences of length 128 (based on heuristic that longer isn't necessarily better).  \n   - If parent is available, downsample to 128 or interpolate to 128.  \n   - Break initialization into phases (around 80-95%, 50-60%, 30-40 sec) with early termination if no improvement after 200 steps.  \n\n2. **Core Optimization:**  \n   - For each initial sequence, perform gradient refinement until the time limit.  \n   - Use momentum in gradient descent to speed convergence and smoothness in the convolution gradient.  \n\n**Search Choices and Variations:**  \n- **Fixed Length:** Use 128 regardless of parent length to balance diversity and computation.  \n- **Time Budget Allocation:**  \n  - **Initialization (Phase 1):** 600 seconds.  \n  - **Gradient Refinement (Phase 2):** 700 seconds.  \n  - **Fallback:** If candidate peaks before evaluation, use simplex fallback.  \n- **Seed and Parent:** Use `height_sequence_1` as a starting point if available, but override with trial-specific seeds.  \n\n**Computing Budget and Robustness:**  \n- **Total Time:** 1600 seconds.  \n- **Phases:**  \n  - **Initialization:** Test up to 10 starting sequences.  \n  - **Gradient Refinement:** For each candidate, refine for up to 1600 seconds.  \n- **Fallback:** Create a fallback sequence of length 128 with uniform coefficients.  \n- **Termination:** Common exit on either time-out or detection of a local minimum.  \n\n**Hybrid Optimizations:**  \n1. **Discrete/Continuous ADMM (Gradient-Free):**  \n   - Use ADMM for optimization without requiring exact gradients, but use the `fast_convolve` function.  \n   - Rationale: Convex relaxations can handle the structure better than pure gradient descent.  \n\n2. **Flow Control:**  \n   - If evaluation becomes too slow with large sequences, truncate to 128.  \n   - Other fallback: Use simple average/median for dimension caching.  \n\n**Advanced Planning:**  \n- **Secondary Goals:** Minimize peaks by design, not just the overall bound.  \n- **Termination:** Stop if improvement stalls after 16 long iterations.  \n- **Monitoring:** Periodically evaluate peak bound to benchmark.",
